      "DENISE: How are you, my sweet girl?\nALIKE: What did you bring me?\nDENISE: Excuse me? It’s not polite to reach for your gift, until it’s offered to you.\nDENISE: Got you something else. It was sent to me by your aunt Jumoke.",
      "ROSALYN: Just friends, huh?\nCLAIRE: It’s complicated.\nROSALYN: When has it ever not been?",
      "USCIS WORKER: I’m not finding any record of your I-539 in the system. You say you sent it in six weeks ago?\nCLAIRE: Eight. Eight weeks.\nUSCIS WORKER: Okay, do you have a mailing receipt?\nCLAIRE: What? No, uh... I just copied my I-94 and sent it by regular mail.",
      "DENISE: I’m pushing for a one on one with the FBI task force officer tomorrow, so if that pans out, I’ll have a better idea of where we stand. Clear…\nROKEYA: When can we see her?",
      "SPECIAL AGENT PHADKAR: Officially, she’s being held for an unlawful presence in the United States. Unoffically, and I’ll never repeat this outside this room, she’s…\nDENISE: And what evidence would that be?\nSPECIAL AGENT PHADKAR: Maybe one day when we amend the constitution and stop granting instant citizenship to the children of illegals, that won’t be an issue. But,…"
    ]
  },
